  "review": [
    "One original node-local gate and wrapped ReadExecutionBudget; metadata/raw/lookahead charged once and complete JSON checked once. Dense window filling checks the same deadline/cancellation for every window.",
    "Latest native descending visit stops after first live sample; baseline and staged merge retain forward fallback signs, exclusive boundaries, byte counters, borrowed lifetimes and disposal. No forward prefix-successor allocation.",
    "Published native Sum/Min/Max receive actual timestamps in canonical order; raw count comes from DataCount and raw average from sum/count. Dense UTC windows retain null maximum end and pre-allocation caps; finite overflow rejects safely.",
    "HTTP and MCP new canonical routes share existing heavy-read ingress capacity. SDK/MCP RF3 tests use independently expected raw results and genuine persisted credentials; revoked credentials reject official calls with HTTP401 before operation dispatch.",
    "Shared request/read actors, RF3 voter topology, node-local storage, persisted policies, inclusive existing read contract and old numeric kinds are preserved.",
    "Independent current dashboard source is included in the requested full working-tree scope. Its current compile inputs were present and unchanged during the final25-project development build; browser/runtime qualification is separate."
